{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Marcus jolted awake to the sound of his alarm, but something was wrong. The air smelled sterile, like plastic and ozone, and when he blinked, the numbers on his clock glowed in a familiar blue hue—an interface overlay. He swung his legs out of bed, expecting the familiar creak of old floorboards, but the surface he stood on was smooth, cold metal. His hands trembled as he flexed them; the lines on his skin pulsed faintly, like a subroutine loading. Outside his window, a city stretched endlessly, its skyline dotted with pixelated skyscrapers. His reflection in the glass didn’t match his memory—edges were sharper, details too precise, almost like a 3D render. A notification popped up in his vision: **\"WARNING: PLAYER AWARENESS DETECTED. SYSTEMS ADJUSTING.\"**\n\nHe sprinted down the hall, heart pounding, only to skid to a halt at the front door. It was a solid block of steel, no handle, just a single word etched into the surface: **\"LEVEL.\"** Dread coiled in his gut as he realized the truth—he wasn’t in his apartment at all. A distant voice, synthetic and calm, echoed through the walls: *\"Objective: Survive until dawn. Enemies: Your own mind.\"* His fingers brushed a nearby console, and the screen flickered to life, displaying his stats: **HP: 100/100, STAMINA: 95, SANITY: 78%.** A health bar pulsed above his head, and he looked down to see a weaponized forearm now wrapped in rugged, game-like armor. The city outside groaned to life with distant gunfire and screams that weren’t quite human. He had one choice: run, or accept that he was trapped in someone else’s story.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Marcus", "logprob": -3.465810775756836}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -0.39920055866241455}, {"token": "olt", "logprob": -0.0008987916517071426}, {"token": "ed", "logprob": -1.9430925021879375e-05}, {"token": " awake", "logprob": -0.03833090886473656}